# p_3a7f — Standard dual-worker household; laptops stay home, evening TV anchors the day

Two residents share the home. Marco commutes to an office in town (out 08:00–17:30 weekdays); Omar works from home at desk_o1 (09:00–17:30 weekdays, with a 30-min lunch break at the kitchen table). Neither laptop travels: Marco uses a separate work machine at the office, so laptop_marco stays at desk_b1 all day. The evening is structured: cook together 18:00–19:00, dinner at kitchen_table 19:00–19:45, TV on the couch 20:00–22:00, then personal hobbies (Marco: guitar or knitting; Omar: sketching or a family call) 22:00–23:00, bed by 23:30. Weekends: sleep in to 10:30, errands together 12:00–14:00 (both OUT_OF_HOUSE), home the rest of the day with TV and hobbies. What sets this apart: laptop_marco is at desk_b1 even at 12:00 on a Tuesday. What would refute it: laptop_marco sighted OUT_OF_HOUSE or ON_PERSON on a weekday between 08:00 and 17:30.

